# Generating content

{% mark class="http-post" %}{% icon name="north_east" /%}`POST`{% /mark %} `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent`

Generates a model response given an input [`GenerateContentRequest`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#request-body).
Refer to the [text generation
guide](/docs/text-generation) for detailed
usage information. Input capabilities differ between models, including
tuned models. Refer to the [model
guide](/docs/models) and [tuning
guide](/docs/model-tuning) for details.

{% two-column-layout %}
  {% left-column %}
## Parameters  {% class="hide-from-toc" id="parameters" %}

  {% section class="api-ref-property-list" %}
  **model**: {% mark %}required{% /mark %} `string`

  The model ID, for example `gemini-2.5-flash`. Forms the resource name `models/{model}`.

  {% /section %}

## Request Body  {% class="hide-from-toc" id="request-body" %}

  {% section class="api-ref-property-list" %}
  **model**: {% mark %}required{% /mark %} `string`

  The name of the `Model` to use for generating the completion. Format: `models/{model}`.

  {% hr /%}

  **contents**: {% mark %}required{% /mark %} [`Content`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Content) `array`

  The content of the current conversation with the model. For single-turn queries, this is a single instance. For multi-turn queries like [chat](/docs/text-generation#multi-turn-conversations), this is a repeated field that contains the conversation history and the latest request.

  {% hr /%}

  **systemInstruction**: [`Content`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Content)

  Optional. Developer set [system instruction(s)](/docs/text-generation#system-instructions). Currently, text only.

  {% hr /%}

  **tools**: [`Tool`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Tool) `array`

  Optional. A list of `Tools` the `Model` may use to generate the next response. A [`Tool`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Tool) is a piece of code that enables the system to interact with external systems to perform an action, or set of actions, outside of knowledge and scope of the `Model`. Supported [`Tool`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Tool)s are `Function` and `code_execution`. Refer to the [Function calling](/docs/function-calling) and the [Code execution](/docs/code-execution) guides to learn more.

  {% hr /%}

  {% details %}
  {% summary %}
  **toolConfig**: `ToolConfig`

  Optional. Tool configuration for any [`Tool`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Tool) specified in the request. Refer to the [Function calling guide](/docs/function-calling#function_calling_modes) for a usage example.

  {% /summary %}

  {% details %}
  {% summary %}
  **functionCallingConfig**: `FunctionCallingConfig`

  Optional. Function calling config.

  {% /summary %}

  {% details %}
  {% summary %}
  **mode**: `string enum`

  Optional. Specifies the mode in which function calling should execute. If unspecified, the default value will be set to AUTO.

  {% /summary %}

  Possible values:

  - `MODE_UNSPECIFIED`: Unspecified function calling mode. This value should not be used.
  - `AUTO`: Default model behavior, model decides to predict either a function call or a natural language response.
  - `ANY`: Model is constrained to always predicting a function call only. If "allowed_function_names" are set, the predicted function call will be limited to any one of "allowed_function_names", else the predicted function call will be any one of the provided "function_declarations".
  - `NONE`: Model will not predict any function call. Model behavior is same as when not passing any function declarations.
  - `VALIDATED`: Model decides to predict either a function call or a natural language response, but will validate function calls with constrained decoding. If "allowed_function_names" are set, the predicted function call will be limited to any one of "allowed_function_names", else the predicted function call will be any one of the provided "function_declarations".

  {% /details %}

  **allowedFunctionNames**: `string array`

  Optional. A set of function names that, when provided, limits the functions the model will call. This should only be set when the Mode is ANY or VALIDATED. Function names should match [FunctionDeclaration.name]. When set, model will predict a function call from only allowed function names.

  {% /details %}

  {% details %}
  {% summary %}
  **retrievalConfig**: `RetrievalConfig`

  Optional. Retrieval config.

  {% /summary %}

  {% details %}
  {% summary %}
  **latLng**: `LatLng`

  Optional. The location of the user.

  {% /summary %}

  **latitude**: `number`

  The latitude in degrees. It must be in the range [-90.0, +90.0].

  **longitude**: `number`

  The longitude in degrees. It must be in the range [-180.0, +180.0].

  {% /details %}

  **languageCode**: `string`

  Optional. The language code of the user. Language code for content. Use language tags defined by [BCP47](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/bcp/bcp47.txt).

  {% /details %}

  **includeServerSideToolInvocations**: `boolean`

  Optional. If true, the API response will include the server-side tool calls and responses within the [`Content`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:Content) message. This allows clients to observe the server's tool interactions.

  {% /details %}

  {% hr /%}

  **safetySettings**: [`SafetySetting`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:SafetySetting) `array`

  Optional. A list of unique [`SafetySetting`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:SafetySetting) instances for blocking unsafe content. This will be enforced on the `GenerateContentRequest.contents` and `GenerateContentResponse.candidates`. There should not be more than one setting for each `SafetyCategory` type. The API will block any contents and responses that fail to meet the thresholds set by these settings. This list overrides the default settings for each `SafetyCategory` specified in the safety_settings. If there is no [`SafetySetting`](/api-reference/generate-content/generate-content#Resource:SafetySetting) for a given `SafetyCategory` provided in the list, the API will use the default safety setting for that category. Harm categories HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH, HARM_CATEGORY_SEXUALLY_EXPLICIT, HARM_CATEGORY_DANGEROUS_CONTENT, HARM_CATEGORY_HARASSMENT, HARM_CATEGORY_CIVIC_INTEGRITY, HARM_CATEGORY_JAILBREAK are supported. Refer to the [guide](/docs/safety-settings) for detailed information on available safety settings. Also refer to the [Safety guidance](/docs/safety-guidance) to learn how to incorporate safety considerations in your AI applications.

  {% hr /%}

  {% details %}
  {% summary %}
  **generationConfig**: `GenerationConfig`

  Optional. Configuration options for model generation and outputs.

  {% /summary %}

  **candidateCount**: `integer`

  Optional. Number of generated responses to return. If unset, this will default to 1. Please note that this doesn't work for previous generation models (Gemini 1.0 family)

  **stopSequences**: `string array`

  Optional. The set of character sequences (up to 5) that will stop output generation. If specified, the API will stop at the first appearance of a `stop_sequence`. The stop sequence will not be included as part of the response.

  **maxOutputTokens**: `integer`

  Optional. The maximum number of tokens to include in a response candidate. Note: The default value varies by model, see the `Model.output_token_limit` attribute of the `Model` returned from the `getModel` function.

  **temperature**: `number`

  Optional. Controls the randomness of the output. Note: The default value varies by model, see the `Model.temperature` attribute of the `Model` returned from the `getModel` function. Values can range from [0.0, 2.0]. This field is no longer supported and is silently ignored on Gemini 3.6 Flash and newer models.

  **topP**: `number`

